                rdfs:subClassOf hume:Component ;
                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Torch Component"@en ;
                :elucidation "A component that is part of a spray torch, such as the combustion chamber or the nozzle."@en .


###  https://www.cobrain-project.eu/ontology/cobrain#Tribometer
:Tribometer rdf:type owl:Class ;
            rdfs:subClassOf :CharacterisationDevice ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Tribometer"@en ;
            :elucidation "A tribometer is a precision scientific instrument that measures tribological quantities, specifically the coefficient of friction, friction force, and wear volume, between two surfaces in relative motion."@en .


###  https://www.cobrain-project.eu/ontology/cobrain#Turntable
:Turntable rdf:type owl:Class ;
           rdfs:subClassOf hume:Device ;
           rdfs:comment """Turntables can feature simple continuous rotation or be synchronized with the manipulator.
Turntables can also be used to coat planar substrates of limited lateral width to achieve higher relative torch/substrate linear velocities than woukd be possible through the linear motion of the manipulator in front of a stationary substrate."""@en ;
           rdfs:isDefinedBy "EN 1395-6:2007: Thermal spraying - Acceptance inspection of thermal spraying equipment - Part 6: Manipulator systems." ;
           rdfs:seeAlso "Anon. (2013), Introduction to Coating Design and Processing, in: R.C. Tucker jr. (Ed.), ASM Handbook Vol. 5A: Thermal Spray Technology, ASM International, Materials Park, OH, USA." ;
           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Mandrel"@en ;
           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Turntable"@en ;
           :elucidation "The turntable is a rotating device in a thermal spray system onto which the tool holding the substrate(s) is mounted."@en .


###  https://www.cobrain-project.eu/ontology/cobrain#Velocity
:Velocity rdf:type owl:Class ;
          rdfs:subClassOf hume:Property ;
          rdfs:isDefinedBy "ISO 80000-3:2019" ;
          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Velocity"@en ;
          :elucidation "Vector quantity corresponding to the rate of change of position"@en .


###  https://www.cobrain-project.eu/ontology/cobrain#VickersHardness
:VickersHardness rdf:type owl:Class ;
                 rdfs:subClassOf :Hardness ;
                 rdfs:seeAlso """ISO 6507-1:2018
ISO 6507-2:2018
ISO 6507-3:2018
ISO 6507-4:2018
ISO 4516:2002""" ;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Vickers Hardness"@en ;
                 :elucidation """Vickers microhardness is specifically defined as the ratio between the maximum load (F, expressed in kgf) applied onto a Vickers indenter and the lateral surface area (Ar) of the residual impression left in the indented material after complete unloading (in mm2). The latter is computed from the length of the diagonals of the residual impression, measured with an optical microscope.
Vickers hardness is specifically told into:
- Vickers hardness: F ≥ 49.03 N (5 kgf)
- Low-force Vickers hardness: 1.961 N (200 gf) ≤ F < 49.03 N (5 kgf)
- Vickers micro-hardness: 0.009807 N (1 gf) ≤ F < 1.961 N (200 gf)"""@en .


###  https://www.cobrain-project.eu/ontology/cobrain#VolumeFlowFeeder
:VolumeFlowFeeder rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf :PowderFeeder ;
                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Volume Flow Feeder"@en ;
                  :elucidation "A powder feeder that meters a defined volume of powder per unit time (e.g. by a rotating grooved disc or a screw), so that the resulting mass flow depends on the bulk density of the powder."@en .


